{"strongs": "H2442", "word": "חָכָה", "translit": "cha.khah", "root": "חכה", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "wait, await", "definition": "[ חָכָה ] verb wait, await — Qal Participle pl construct חוֺכֵי Isa 30:18 with לְ waiting for him ( ׳ י ). Pi`el חִכָּה Job 32:4 חִכְּתָה Ps 33:20 חִכִּיתִי Isa 8:17 חִכּוּ Ps 106:13 חִכִּינוּ 2Kgs 7:9 Imperfect יְחַכֶּה Isa 30:18 תְּחַכֶּה 2Kgs 9:3 Imperative חַכֵּהֿ Hab 2:3 חִכּוּ Zeph 3:8 Infinitive construct כְּחַכֵּי Hos 6:9 ( Ephr for חַכֵּה ?); Participle מְחַכֶּה Dan 12:12 construct מְחַכֵּה Isa 64:3 plural מְחַכִּים Job 3:21 — 1. wait, tarry , absolute 2Kgs 9:3 tarry not ; with עַד till morning light 2Kgs 7:9 with accusative את איוב בדברים Job 32:4 tarry for Job with words. 2. wait (in ambush), כְּחַכֵּי אִישׁ גְּדוּדִים Hos 6:9 as marauding bands wait for a man AV RV De , or as marauders lie in wait Hi Ew (taking אישׁ as construct) 3 wait for, long for , with לְ for ׳ י Isa 8:17 ; Isa 64:3 ; Zeph 3:8 ; Ps 33:20 for his counsel Ps 106:13 for his vision Hab 2:3 for death Job 3:21 יחכה יהוה לחננכם Yahweh waiteth to be gracious unto you Isa 30:18 ( Di regards this as threatening and refers it to 1 ); absolute waiteth (and cometh to the days of blessedness) Dan 12:12 . חַכָּה see below חנך .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2728')\">BDB2728</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2442')\">H2442</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2727')\">BDB2727</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2729')\">BDB2729</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>חָכָה</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>wait, await</highlightword> — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Participle pl</highlight> construct <bdbheb>חוֺכֵי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 30:18\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(23,30,18)\">Isa 30:18</ref> with <bdbheb>לְ</bdbheb> <highlight>waiting for him</highlight> (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb>). <b>Pi`el</b> <bdbheb>חִכָּה</bdbheb>